course: dictionary
lesson: 9383
title: Spotty and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Spotty» is a good example. Its first meaning is covered with spots or dots, as in «a spotty dress».
explain: Look at the words around it. In «the spotty coat hides it in the dappled shade of trees and long grass», spotty describes a coat with spots, and the hiding tells you the spots help the leopard blend in. Ask: which meaning fits here?
explain: The second meaning is about skin with pimples, as in «spotty skin». A third meaning, mainly US, is uneven: good in some places and bad in others, like «a spotty signal». Swap your chosen meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Spotty means covered with spots or dots.
fact: Spotty can mean having pimples on the skin.
fact: Spotty (mainly US) can mean not even or not regular, good in some places and bad in others.
fact: The forms are spotty, spottier and spottiest, so a signal can be spottier than before.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of spotty the writer means.
exercise: In «a spotty snake that hisses sh-sh», what does spotty mean? | Not even, good in some places and bad in others | Having pimples on the skin | Very fast | *Covered with spots or dots
exercise: Ella says, «The phone has a spotty signal on the train.» What does spotty mean here? | Covered in dots like a dress | *Good in some places and bad in others | Having pimples | Smooth and clear all the way
exercise: Which sentence uses spotty to mean having pimples on the skin? | The leopard's spotty coat hides it in the long grass. | The spotty signal dropped out on the bus. | The spotty dress had red dots on blue. | *Her spotty skin was sore, so she saw a doctor.
test: A leopard's «spotty coat» helps it hide in the dappled shade. What does spotty mean? | Having pimples on the skin | Shiny and smooth | Not even, good in some places and bad in others | *Covered with spots or dots
test: Dad says the Wi-Fi is spotty in the garden, but fine in the kitchen. What does spotty mean? | *Not even, good in some places and bad in others | Covered with spots | Very quiet | Having pimples
exam: Which meaning of spotty fits best in «the spotty coat hides it in the dappled shade of trees and long grass»? | Old and worn | Having pimples on the skin | Not even, good in some places and bad in others | *Covered with spots or dots
